      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LEGASELLI (6) deserves another shot at the 1600m, where she's unbeaten. Struggled to see the 2000m out after displaying a poor post-race recovery with a tiring tenth at Kembla Grange. Apprentice claim and tongue-tie should see her bounce back quickly. OURAGAN (3) has solid recent form and should get a comfortable lead from the sticky gate. Kept finding with a tidy second again over this trip at Hawkesbury. Top three contender deep into the campaign. AUTUMN SKY (2) was held up along the inside and peaked on the run first-up in a BM64 over 1300m at Illawarra Grange. Assess on the good debut victory over 1250m at Newcastle last March. Jumps sharply in trip and not to be underestimated with the claim. DERRY CITY FELIX (5) was mediocre at 2000m last time but could rebound with a drop to 1600m, weight relief, and a prior Hawkesbury third giving him a genuine chance if he recaptures that form. Something for the Multiples: OVERSHADOW (1)",
